  "result": "I found the cause of the clamping bug and wrote a fix plan, but haven't changed any code yet. The usual \"approve plan\" step isn't available here, so please reply to approve it.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py:754` returns `bound - dir`. It should return `bound + dir`. The caller passes `dir=1` for the minimum and `dir=-1` for the maximum, which is the direction to step back inside the range. So when a bound is open (excluded), the code steps the wrong way and lands outside the range:\n\n- `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-3` returns `-1`; it should return `1`.\n- `IntRange(0, 5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` given `9` returns `6`; it should return `4`.\n\nRanges whose bounds are included aren't affected, which is why the existing tests pass.\n\n**Plan:**\n1. Change `return bound - dir` to `return bound + dir` at `src/click/types.py:754`.\n2. Add four open-bound clamp cases to the `test_range` list in `tests/test_types.py`: values below and above the range, plus a value sitting exactly on each excluded bound.\n3. Run `pytest tests/test_types.py`, then the full test suite.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-optimized-rain.md`.",
